Kibble Dispenser - licensing

Copyright 2026 Enrico Icardi and contributors

This project uses three permissive licences, one for each kind of file. Together they allow
anyone, the author included, to build, modify, fork and sell the dispenser or products
derived from it, as long as the copyright and licence notices are kept (and, for the
documentation and photos, credit is given).

1. Software: MIT License (LICENSES/MIT.txt)
   - firmware/ (ESPHome configuration and any future firmware code)
   - hardware/cad/*.py (CAD generator and check scripts)
   - site/ (website code), except site/index.html (see 3); the bundled three.js library in
     site/vendor/three/ is MIT too, copyright 2010-2023 three.js authors
   - CI, templates and configuration files (.github/, .gitignore, .gitattributes, REUSE.toml)

2. Hardware design files: CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive
   (LICENSES/CERN-OHL-P-2.0.txt)
   - hardware/stl/ and hardware/3mf/ (part geometry)
   - hardware/assembly/ (assembly-frame meshes and data for the 3D viewer)
   - hardware/cad/*.json (layout and drivetrain design data)

3. Documentation and photos: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
   (LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt)
   - docs/ (build guide, research notes, photos)
   - README.md files and other Markdown prose
   - site/index.html (the text of the website)
   - CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md is adapted from the Contributor Covenant 2.1, also under CC BY 4.0

The exact licence and copyright of every path are listed in REUSE.toml, following the
REUSE specification (https://reuse.software). If REUSE.toml and this summary ever
disagree, REUSE.toml is authoritative.
